  ],
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\group.action:of{G ::= (Y, *, e)}:on{X}]\nDeclares: alpha(g_, x_) is \\function:on{Y \\.set.cross./ X}:to{X}\nwhen:\n. G is \\group\n. X is \\set\nsatisfies:\n. forAll: x \"in\" X\n  then: alpha(e, x) = x\n. forAll: g, h \"in\" G\n  then:\n  . forAll: x \"in\" X\n    then: alpha(g * h, x) = alpha(g, alpha(h, x))\nDocumented:\n. called: \"group action of $G?$ on $X?$\"\n. writing: alpha(g_, x_)\n  as: \"g_? \\cdot x_?\"\n. description: \"A left action represents each group element as a symmetry of the\n                set and respects identity and multiplication.\"\nId: \"fa043cd6-0ce8-4504-82bb-aba9ad2c8a30\"",
